            <ArticleTitle>Is there a role for acupuncture in the treatment of tendinopathy?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/acupmed-2012-010208</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tendinopathy is a debilitating condition in athletic and sedentary populations for which a gold standard treatment strategy does not yet exist. While the pathophysiology of tendinopathy is well understood, a debate remains as to the nature of the pain mechanism in tendinopathy which makes treatment selection challenging. This clinical discussion presents evidence to suggest that acupuncture may have a role in the treatment of tendinopathy, through the facilitation of tendon blood flow and fibroblastic activity, making recommendations for further research.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
